            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marwadi for to smash, then the Marwadi for to get cross."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: खरो",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "खरो — kharo — \"correct; genuine\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "थारो जवाब खरो है। thāro javāb kharo hai. Your answer is correct."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "खरो (kharo) is inherited from Sanskrit khara, \"hard, sharp\"; CDIAL lists Old Marwari kharaü, \"extreme\", Sindhi kharo, \"pure, genuine\", and Gujarati kharũ, \"real, good\" (CDIAL 3819). How the sense \"correct\" grew out of \"hard\" is not settled. It agrees like any -ो adjective: खरो जवाब, खरी बात."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for asking and answering."
            }
          ]
        },
